# What the checker reads. `lib/` is the code that ships and the only code this
# repository holds to `typed: strict`; `sorbet/rbi/` is the generated
# definitions for the gems it reaches, plus the hand-written shims.
#
# `spec/` is deliberately out of scope. RSpec defines its helpers with `def`
# inside blocks, which Sorbet reads as methods on `Object` -- one spec's
# `def initialize(root:)` is enough to make `Object.new` a type error in
# `lib/`. Checking the suite would cost the accuracy of checking the library.
--dir
lib
--dir
sorbet/rbi
#
# `requires_ancestor` is how the three modules that are extended into
# something else -- Sources::Definition above all -- say what they are extended
# into, which is the only way `raise` and `superclass` resolve inside them. It
# is still behind a flag upstream.
--enable-experimental-requires-ancestor
--ignore=tmp/
--ignore=vendor/
--parser=prism
